# Gradle cache quarantine policy (incident response only — keep EMPTY in steady state).
#
# Each non-comment line names one gradle/actions extracted-entry bundle whose cache RESTORE is
# skipped fleet-wide (GRADLE_BUILD_ACTION_SKIP_RESTORE). Allowlisted bundle names only:
#   dependencies
#   transforms
# A quarantine line must stay until the poisoned bundle key rotates naturally (its file-set
# changes) — removing it earlier lets the poisoned entry restore again. This is a targeted
# quarantine, not a purge: the poisoned entry itself remains in the backend until eviction.
# Epoch rotation lives in .github/gradle-cache-epoch (single line, no comments).
# Operating procedure: docs/ci-gradle-cache-epoch-runbook.md
